checkout: /Users/Rajeev/Workspace/kitchen-management-system

WHY THIS IS NOT AN INVERTED CONTROL, AND IS NOT PRETENDING TO BE ONE
====================================================================
A control normally patches the change back out and shows the tests go red. A removal cannot
do that honestly: putting `startRecurringPlan` back would only prove that a test asserting its
absence fails when it is present, which is a tautology dressed as evidence. Manufacturing one
would be worse than having none.

What is demonstrated instead is the ACCEPTED CONSEQUENCE — the four things that have to be
true for this removal to be the right removal rather than a grep-and-delete:

  C1  the one-time path a devotee actually uses still works, end to end
  C2  no identifier of recurring donations is referenced by any live statement
  C3  the ordinary-English "recurring" elsewhere in the app is untouched
  C4  the removal is real in the tree, not merely unreferenced

C3 is the one that matters most and the one a "grep returns nothing" acceptance would have
failed: `recurring` is ordinary English in the Vaishnava calendar and in the event planner,
and those uses are not this feature.

